// Comparing the fingerprints.
//
// Each function is reported against the *first* function it matches, and the
// one reported is the later of the two -- the same pairing idc.py produces,
// which stops at the first collision it meets while walking the functions in
// order. Every collision is reported rather than only the first, as everywhere
// else in this checker.

uq_scan() {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import cfp))) {
    uq_at(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
given lz_o ():() then calls uq_at:(0) then calls uq_at:(1)
given lz_o ():() then calls uq_at:[2]

// dup5 and dup9 differ in a literal, which the strict fingerprint keeps, so
// neither is reported against the other: the case pins the quiet path, which
// is the one a broken comparison would break first.
uq_at(int i) {
  int j = find_dup(i);
  if(j >= 0) {
    report_dup(i, j);
  }
} return void;
given lz_o (1):() then calls report_dup:[0]
given lz_o (0):() then calls report_dup:[0]

// The first earlier function with the same fingerprint, or -1. The search
// stops at the match: `found < 0` in the condition is how a loop leaves early
// here, and the flag doubles as the answer.
find_dup(int i) {
  int j = 0;
  int found = 0 - 1;
  while(j < i && found < 0) {
    found = dup_probe(i, j);
    j = j + 1;
  }
} return int found;
